# Awoof Academic Profile Retention Purge Cron Template
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS: INSTALLED ON PRODUCTION 2026-10-19 (owner-approved 30-day window).
# This file remains the reviewed template; the installed crontab line uses
# the production host's log directory (/home/bassey/awoof-logs).
#
# PURPOSE:
# Daily scheduled execution of the academic profile data cleanup script to purge
# academic profiles belonging to soft-deleted accounts whose deletion occurred
# at or before the approved retention cutoff (ACADEMIC_PROFILE_RETENTION_DAYS).
#
# PREREQUISITES BEFORE ACTIVATION:
# 1. Legal and management authorization of ACADEMIC_PROFILE_RETENTION_DAYS (e.g. 30).
# 2. ACADEMIC_PROFILE_RETENTION_DAYS set in production environment (.env / systemd).
# 3. Migration 088 applied (providing academic_profile_deletion_ledger and generation_id).
# 4. The backend container's backups volume (backend_backups, mounted at /usr/src/app/backups) is provisioned so tombstones land in the same durable ledger the API appends to.
#
# HOSTINGER VPS INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:
# Supported form (Container execution via crontab for deploy user):
#   crontab -e
#   Add the line below (uncommented):
#   30 3 * * * docker exec -i -u nodejs awoof-backend node dist/scripts/cleanup-academic-profile-data.js --batch-size 500 >> /var/log/awoof/academic-profile-purge.log 2>&1
#
# Host-side execution is intentionally not offered: under
# docker-compose.hostinger.yml the database publishes no host port (its
# DB_HOST name only resolves inside the Compose network), and the durable
# deletion ledger lives in the backend container's backups volume
# (/usr/src/app/backups). A host process could neither reach Postgres nor
# write the ledger that backend startup reconciliation reads, so erased
# profiles could be resurrected by a later restore.
#
# CONCURRENCY AND RESILIENCE:
# - The docker exec form must run as the nodejs user (-u nodejs): the image
#   has no USER instruction, so exec would otherwise run as root and could
#   create the mode-0600 ledger file root-owned, after which API erasures
#   running as nodejs could no longer append their tombstones.
# - Script acquires PostgreSQL session advisory lock (2026101801) on a dedicated connection.
#   If a prior run is still in progress, the overlapping run exits cleanly without error.
# - Deletions are processed in batches (default 500) and recorded in the dual deletion ledger.
# - Outputs counts/outcomes only; never logs PII, emails, or personal identifiers.
#
# TEMPLATE LINE (Uncomment and set correct paths upon activation):
# 30 3 * * * docker exec -i -u nodejs awoof-backend node dist/scripts/cleanup-academic-profile-data.js --batch-size 500 >> /var/log/awoof/academic-profile-purge.log 2>&1
